{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/402467-changeling-sherlock-holmes","id":402467,"title":"Changeling Sherlock Holmes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-11T14:34:01-08:00","id":402467,"title":"Changeling Sherlock Holmes","content":"Hi guys. I was told to try here because I am horrible at doing +sheets. I am looking to create a Changeling who has the skill set of Sherlock Holmes. I have 800xp to play with on this character. Can anyone help me with this? It would be nWoD game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5025-paladine","name":"Paladine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:48:01-08:00","id":402662,"title":"","content":"When you say it's a &quot;nWoD game&quot; you mean it's plain nWoD, no God Machine update?<br /> <br /> Also, for your rendition of Sherlock would I be correct in assuming you want your character to be the best detective they can be and not merely that you want to duplicate the stats of Mr Holmes? I ask because Sherlock Holmes can be pretty reasonably written up as a mortal with just a little extra whereas an 800 exp changeling can do much more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T20:00:23-08:00","id":402851,"title":"","content":"Yes its an nWoD with God Machine update. As for the concept, yes I would like it like Sherlock Holmes skills/talents/merits based but a Changeling Detective overall<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5025-paladine","name":"Paladine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T23:15:22-08:00","id":403075,"title":"","content":"o.O<br /> <br /> So you are using the God Machine update? 800 exp is ALLOT of exp in GMC. It only costs you 292 exp to get EVERY Skill and Attribute to 5 dots. For 757 of your exp you can get Wyrd 10 and every Skill and Attribute at 10!<br /> <br /> I guess to go further I'll need to know what you/your ST is charging for Contracts since the GMC rules aren't out for Changelings yet. <br /> <br /> All in all tho this isn't really a recipe to make Sherlock Holmes. It's a recipe to make a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T11:27:33-08:00","id":403507,"title":"","content":"It's not all GMC rules. Its a combo of GMC and nWoD. They have it modified. 800 gives me a strong canon character based on this game. Or so I am told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5025-paladine","name":"Paladine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T17:06:25-08:00","id":405315,"title":"","content":"At 800 XP in GMC, you are not playing Sherlock Holmes, you're playing the All Seeing Eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T18:30:34-08:00","id":405374,"title":"","content":"I think the main issue is: which experience point costs are you using? The ones listed in the Changeling the Lost book or the ones in the GMC book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T15:59:36-08:00","id":406178,"title":"","content":"Without getting into numbers you'll want high levels of Intelligence, Wits, Investigation, and Science. Computers and Medicine also make sense for electronic forensics and autopsies. Moving into Merits you'll want Professional Training (Investigator) providing 9-again to Investigation and Science. Danger Sense, Direction Sense, Eidetic Memory, Eye for the Strange, and Trained Observer are all also good for detecting things.<br /> <br /> On the Changeling side being Darkling or Fireheart lets you boost Wits pools for Glamour. Other good Kiths include Cleareyes and Whisperwrisp, the former because anything that boosts perception helps with investigation and the later kinda fits as spies need to by able to gather info just like gumshoes. <br /> <br /> Where Contracts are concerned there are allot that can be helpful for information gathering. Dream can let you analyze a subject's dreams to learn about them. Omen can let you get a look at what Fate has planned. Fang and Talon gives some hefty perception bonuses and can let you sense things otherwise invisible such as UV light or getting the smell of a dog. Contracts of Den give perception bonuses in your territory. Shade and Spirit can bring back the dead for questioning. Contracts of Communion can give good intel by letting you track things like bullets or see through the water in someone's sink. Separation makes for some easy B&amp;E, a valuable skill in the PI's toolkit. Oath and Punishment or Four Directions can let you track a target once you know who they are and Oath and Punishment gives other intel on a subject's transgressions as well. Animation lets you talk to objects if you don't have any living witnesses. The Fleeting seasonal Contracts give valuable insight into your subject's emotional state (well except for Summer). Contracts of Spell-bound Autumn lets you analyze magic items. Contracts of Potential give an amazing insight into anyone's actions. Most Goblin Contracts are kinda worthless but Goblin Sight of Truth and Lies is very useful when trying to suss out the truth at any cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}